==============================================================================
Code ported from rvt-rs
==============================================================================

Parts of this crate are ported from rvt-rs, an open reader for Autodesk Revit
files, https://github.com/DrunkOnJava/rvt-rs, which carries this notice:

    rvt-rs: open reader for Autodesk Revit files
    Copyright 2026 Griffin Long

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

The version ported from is commit b6086d41b9758fd9b92f42f0a47b8345b9c58056
(after the v0.6.1 tag). What was taken, and from which file, is listed module by
module in docs/rvt-provenance.md. Every source file that holds ported code names
its rvt-rs source file and that commit in a header, and states that it was
changed: the code was rewritten for BIMCraft (no panics, explicit size limits,
no dependencies beyond cfb, flate2 and memchr, a different structure), and the
format findings it applies were checked again on sample files.

This notice carries only what Apache License 2.0 section 4(d) asks of a
derivative work: rvt-rs's attribution notices. Its statements about the legal
basis of reverse engineering are its own and are not repeated here; see
docs/rvt-provenance.md for how this project states the risk.

==============================================================================
Trademarks
==============================================================================

"Autodesk" and "Revit" are registered trademarks of Autodesk, Inc. This project
is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Autodesk. The names appear
only to identify the file format this reader parses.

This crate contains no Autodesk source code, object code, SDK components or
header files, and no content taken from inside an Autodesk file (families,
templates, icons, help text). It reads a file the user gives it and never
bundles or extracts assets for the project.

==============================================================================
Third-party dependencies
==============================================================================

  cfb      MIT              reads the Compound File (OLE) container
  flate2   MIT OR Apache-2.0  inflates Revit's gzip streams
  memchr   Unlicense OR MIT   byte search

See each dependency's own licence for its terms.

Plugins run in wasmi, a WebAssembly interpreter in Rust (MIT OR Apache-2.0);
its own dependencies are wasmi_core, wasmi_ir and wasmi_collections (MIT OR
Apache-2.0), wasmparser (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT),
hashbrown (MIT OR Apache-2.0), foldhash (Zlib), spin (MIT), string-interner
(MIT OR Apache-2.0), leb128fmt (MIT OR Apache-2.0), bumpalo (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
and libm (MIT). The guest SDK (crates/plugin-sdk) has no runtime of its own.

