==============================================================================
Map coordinate systems: EPSG, crs-definitions and proj4rs
==============================================================================

The core (bimcraft-core) converts a project's shared coordinates to WGS84
through two crates, unmodified:

  crs-definitions  CC0-1.0            EPSG's CRS definitions as proj strings
    https://crates.io/crates/crs-definitions/0.6.0
  proj4rs          MIT OR Apache-2.0  map projections, a Rust PROJ.4
    https://crates.io/crates/proj4rs/0.3.0

The definitions come from the EPSG Geodetic Parameter Dataset, maintained by
the International Association of Oil & Gas Producers (IOGP), https://epsg.org,
used under its terms of use. BIMCraft names each system by its EPSG code and
name as the dataset gives them; it does not change the dataset's data.

==============================================================================
World map: Natural Earth
==============================================================================

The Coordinates window's offline world map (assets/map/world.bin) is drawn
from Natural Earth's 1:110m land polygons and land borders, packed smaller and
rounded to hundredths of a degree. Made with Natural Earth. Free vector and
raster map data @ naturalearthdata.com. Natural Earth is in the public domain.
  https://github.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector

The places a map system is found by (assets/map/places.tsv) are Natural Earth's
1:50m countries (with their names in several languages) and 1:10m populated
places, their names and positions only. Made with Natural Earth.

